# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# What never reaches the build context.
#
# A .dockerignore miss is not just a bigger image — every excluded line here is
# something that would otherwise be readable inside a container that holds Admin
# SDK credentials. The list mirrors `functions.ignore` in firebase.json, which
# already drops node_modules, **/*.test.js and vitest.config.js for the same
# reasons, so the two deploy surfaces stay ignorable by the same rules.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Installed fresh from the lockfile inside the image. Copying the host's tree
# would drag a Windows/macOS install into a Linux image — firebase-admin's gRPC
# stack is the usual casualty — and would do it silently, because the files are
# there and only fail at require time.
node_modules

# Secrets, first and loudest. Nothing in server/ has one today; this line is
# here so that the day somebody adds server/.env it does not become a layer in
# a pushed image, where it stays readable forever even if the next commit
# deletes the file. Cloud Run gets its configuration from the environment and
# its credentials from the metadata server. Neither is ever baked in.
.env
.env.*

# Tests and their config. vitest is not installed in the image (--omit=dev), so
# these could not run there anyway — and they are a precise written description
# of which checks guard which write, which is not something to ship to anyone
# who pulls the image.
**/*.test.js
vitest.config.js

# Docs and build inputs — the image is not where anyone reads these.
README.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Local noise that has no meaning inside a container.
.git
.gitignore
*.log
npm-debug.log*
coverage
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Vitest writes these transient snapshots next to its config (see the repo's
# .gitignore, same entry, same reason).
vitest.config.js.timestamp-*
